Objective
To create a Jenkins pipeline that pulls a Docker image from Docker Hub and runs it as a container.

Step 1: Open Jenkins Dashboard
Go to http://localhost:8080 and login.

Step 2: Create a New Pipeline Job
- Click on 'New Item'
- Enter job name: simple-pipeline
- Select 'Pipeline'
- Click OK

Step 3: Open Docker Desktop 

Step 4: Configure Jenkins Pipeline
pipeline {
    agent any
    
    stages {
        stage('Check Docker') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker --version'
            }
        }
        stage('Pull Docker Image') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker pull nginx'
            }
        }
        stage('Run Container') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker run -d -p 8085:80 --name my-nginx nginx'
            }
        }
        stage('Verify Container') {

            steps {
                bat 'docker ps'
            }
        }
    }
}

Step 5: Run Pipeline

Click Build Now

Step 6: Verify Output
Open browser and go to: http://localhost:8085
